<div class="spr-welcome">
  <span class="spr-welcome-mark"><%~ it.mark_icon %></span>
  <h1>Welcome to Speicher.md</h1>
  <p>
    Speicher.md publishes the Markdown files in your Git repositories as a documentation site. People sign in with
    the accounts they already have, such as Microsoft Entra ID, Google or GitHub, and each page is shown only to the
    people its repository grants access to. AI assistants can search and read the same pages, with the same
    permissions, through the MCP server of Speicher.md.
  </p>
  <% if (it.finished) { %>
  <%~ include('@note', { level: 'ok', html: md('The setup of this instance is complete. All settings remain available under [Configuration](/-/config).') }) %>
  <% } else { %>
  <p>
    This setup guides you through a few steps: you connect a sign-in, become the administrator, create groups and
    publish your first repository. To begin, click the button at the bottom of the page.
  </p>
  <% } %>
</div>
